# env / secrets
# Catch-all: `.env` and `.env.*.local` alone missed real credential files such
# as `.env.vercel` (DATABASE_URL / SUPABASE keys / VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN), which
# therefore showed up as untracked and was one `git add -A` away from being
# published. Ignore every .env variant and allow-list the committed samples.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
!*.env.example

